# =============================================================================
#  Docker build context  —  WO-22 (PKG-05)
# =============================================================================
#  Both images build from the repository root, so this one file governs both.
#
#  This is not only a speed optimisation. Next's standalone output tracer copies
#  whatever it finds next to the app, and it was verified to pull `.env.local`
#  and the `apps/web/.env` symlink straight into `.next/standalone/`. Without
#  the env rules below, a built image would carry the production Neon URL and
#  JWT_SECRET in a layer — readable by anyone who can `docker pull` it, and
#  still readable after a later layer deletes the file.
# =============================================================================

# --- Secrets. Keep this block first and do not weaken it. --------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.render.example
!.env.vercel.example
.envrc
.sentryclirc
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
credentials/

# --- Database dumps: member PII, and large. ----------------------------------
backups/
*.dump
*.dump.gpg
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Reinstalled inside the image from the lockfile. -------------------------
node_modules
**/node_modules
.pnpm-store

# --- Build outputs. A host .next/ leaking in produces a container serving a
#     stale build that no source change explains. ----------------------------
.next
**/.next
out
dist
build
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# --- Go build artefacts. Rebuilt in the builder stage. -----------------------
bin/
apps/api/server
apps/api/app
**/*.test
**/*.out

# --- Not needed to build or run. ---------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github
.githooks
.gitleaks.toml
docs
*.md
!apps/web/README.md
LICENSE
test-results
playwright-report
playwright/.cache
coverage
.vscode
.idea
.claude
.agents
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
